&lt;h2&gt;About Lucerne Publishing&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lucerne Publishing makes reading apps for schools and libraries. Our digital team builds the apps teachers and students open every day, and the services behind them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#x27;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build features in TypeScript and React with a senior engineer beside you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write tests for what you ship, and fix what they find&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Join planning and design reviews from your first week&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#x27;ll need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JavaScript or TypeScript, from work, school or your own projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with Git and code review&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A degree in computer science or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;React Native&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Accessibility work&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is hybrid, three days a week in our New York, NY office. The salary range is $80,000&amp;ndash;$95,000.&lt;/p&gt;
